{:id :constraint/ttms-compacts-by-support-dominance
 :type :constraint
 :created-at #inst "2026-09-29T20:34:26Z"
 :scope "Module boundary: opt-in TTMS support sets, evidence merge, and strongest projection; existing distributed-TMS retention remains unchanged."
 :direct-tags [:tag/truth-maintenance :tag/partial-information :tag/projection]
 :applies-to [:component/cell-semantics :component/truth-maintenance]
 :supersedes [:constraint/merge-never-silently-deletes-evidence]
 :text "1. A premise contains exactly :source, :timestamp, and :premises-status. Source is the injection cell's NodeId; status is :active or :retracted. Derived computations preserve source IDs and timestamps. 2. Support N covers O iff every premise in O has a premise in N with the same source and either a greater timestamp under timestamp/time-rank or equal timestamp rank and equal status. 3. N dominates O iff N is compatible (each source has one timestamp/status pair), N covers O, and either O does not cover N or O is incompatible. Base values do not participate in this comparison. 4. Evidence merge unions observation sets and removes an observation only when another observation's support dominates it. Exception: source-free nothing is discarded when nonbottom evidence exists. Equal-support observations with different bases remain. 5. Strongest excludes stale payloads using current source timestamps, merges eligible bases through existing cell merge, and retains their complete support together with current source states. Incompatible support must not be normalized into compatible support to make a computation usable. Conflicting eligible bases produce contradiction without losing those dependencies. 6. Any retracted premise makes the projected datum unusable. Equal-valued independent sources remain conjunctively required; retracting one must not silently fall back to another. 7. This rule does not authorize changing the runner, compiler defaults, compound synchronization, or existing distributed-TMS retention. Existing distributed TMS continues to preserve accumulated claims and provenance, with premise state controlling strongest projection."
 :verification "Validate source-ID specs and lookup through two computations; test coverage and dominance including active/retracted states; test merge associativity, commutativity and idempotence on normalized evidence, exact contradiction support, stale replay, retraction/reactivation, and all enumerated diamond schedules. Separately run existing TMS and event regressions. Finite checks do not establish unrestricted convergence."
 :evidence-state :needs-verification}
